  "summary": "You follow the joint MS (with an MBA or JD) or the dual MS (with another Stanford degree), and either way you need 45 units for this MS: ENVRES 280 and 290, one human environmental decision-making course, four courses from one of the six pathways, and electives numbered 100 or above, with at most 12 professional school units, 5 guest-lecture units and 5 individual study units (8 for the dual MS). The core, decision-making and pathway courses must be letter graded, and the decision-making and pathway courses carry at least 3 units each; the pathway courses count toward the 45 units. Your advisor checks the 23 units at the 200 level and the 3.0 GPA, because your other degree's courses are on the same record, and a science methods course used for decision-making is moved in by hand.",
